{"audit_findings": "```json
{
  "analysis_summary": "This ontology demonstrates a solid structural foundation with proper segment typing and relationship modeling. However, it suffers from critical D96A INVOIC incompleteness (~45% segment coverage) and lacks essential qualifier-based semantic distinctions that are mandatory in EANCOM. The model conflates distinct EDIFACT concepts (e.g., all NAD segments treated identically) and omits ~12 required segment types including critical elements like IMD, PAC, ALC, and FTX.",

  "completeness_score": 0.45,

  "extensions_required": [
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "IMDSegment (Item Description)",
      "priority": "high",
      "rationale": "D96A INVOIC Mandatory. Required for item descriptions beyond basic identifiers. Without IMD, you cannot properly describe traded items per EANCOM business rules."
    },
    {
      "type": "class",
      "name": "PACSegment (Package)",
      "priority": "high",
      ", "owl_reviewed_length": 31865, "consultation_logged": true, "audits_remaining": 2}

